1
00:00:12,000 --> 00:00:15,207
- [romantic song intro playing]
- Okay, and for our next song...

2
00:00:15,208 --> 00:00:17,083
Hey, Geng-ming, you're up.

3
00:00:17,625 --> 00:00:19,000
Show them what you got.

4
00:00:22,083 --> 00:00:26,083
[singing in Mandarin]
<i>♪ Lounging on the couch all day ♪</i>

5
00:00:26,958 --> 00:00:30,749
<i>♪ Binge-watching till our eyes are puffy ♪</i>

6
00:00:30,750 --> 00:00:33,207
<i>♪ You cook, I do the dishes ♪</i>

7
00:00:33,208 --> 00:00:35,499
<i>♪ A simple, romantic day ♪</i>

8
00:00:35,500 --> 00:00:40,208
[in unison] <i>♪ Two cute cats ♪</i>

9
00:00:41,041 --> 00:00:43,290
<i>♪ Our cozy little life ♪</i>

10
00:00:43,291 --> 00:00:45,624
<i>♪ We fight, then make up ♪</i>

11
00:00:45,625 --> 00:00:50,165
<i>♪ Tempers rise, then fade ♪</i>

12
00:00:50,166 --> 00:00:52,249
<i>♪ Our hearts melt again ♪</i>

13
00:00:52,250 --> 00:00:54,582
<i>♪ Into a sweet embrace ♪</i>

14
00:00:54,583 --> 00:01:00,290
<i>♪ Crazy in love and happy ♪</i>

15
00:01:00,291 --> 00:01:02,875
[distorted mic feedback buzzes]

16
00:01:03,458 --> 00:01:05,665
[mic feedback screeching]

17
00:01:05,666 --> 00:01:07,958
[whirring]

18
00:01:14,708 --> 00:01:16,416
[menacing music playing]

19
00:01:20,333 --> 00:01:21,916
[music crescendoes]

20
00:01:27,125 --> 00:01:29,125
[opening theme music playing]

21
00:01:56,250 --> 00:01:57,499
MIRACLES OF THE ER

22
00:01:57,500 --> 00:01:59,958
EPISODE 7: TRUTH AND LIES

23
00:02:02,041 --> 00:02:04,790
[Geng-ming breathing shakily]

24
00:02:04,791 --> 00:02:06,375
[somber music playing]

25
00:02:10,375 --> 00:02:11,707
[footsteps approaching]

26
00:02:11,708 --> 00:02:14,582
[EMT in English] Sir, move aside, please.
We'll take it from here.

27
00:02:14,583 --> 00:02:16,290
[panting]

28
00:02:16,291 --> 00:02:18,583
[EMT] Miss. Miss, can you hear me?

29
00:02:22,083 --> 00:02:24,625
All right, let's move. We're losing time.

30
00:02:27,583 --> 00:02:29,583
[breath trembling]

31
00:02:31,208 --> 00:02:33,207
[siren wailing]

32
00:02:33,208 --> 00:02:35,291
[somber music builds]

33
00:02:40,166 --> 00:02:42,040
- [nurse] Trauma blue!
- [EMT] Major trauma.

34
00:02:42,041 --> 00:02:44,374
- Ped struck by vehicle. Massive bleeding.
- [Yuan-ting] Tang Hsi?

35
00:02:44,375 --> 00:02:46,582
[EMT] BP 70 over 50. Heart rate 134.

36
00:02:46,583 --> 00:02:49,499
- Get Dr. He. She's here. Arrange for CT.
- [Yuan-ting] Okay. Got it.

37
00:02:49,500 --> 00:02:51,040
- Bring her through.
- [Su-ching] This way.

38
00:02:51,041 --> 00:02:51,958
What happened?

39
00:02:57,583 --> 00:02:58,416
[door thuds]

40
00:03:01,250 --> 00:03:02,249
[music fades]

41
00:03:02,250 --> 00:03:04,333
[breath trembling]

42
00:03:05,416 --> 00:03:07,415
[Cheng-chun in muffled voice]
<i>Tang Hsi. Can you hear me?</i>

43
00:03:07,416 --> 00:03:08,957
<i>Tang Hsi. Tang Hsi!</i>

44
00:03:08,958 --> 00:03:10,125
[Yuan-ting] <i>Tang Hsi?</i>

45
00:03:10,791 --> 00:03:12,874
<i>- How did this happen?</i>
- [breath trembling]

46
00:03:12,875 --> 00:03:15,582
[Su-ching]
<i>Tang Hsi, wake up. Stay with us, okay?</i>

47
00:03:15,583 --> 00:03:17,457
[Cheng-chun]
<i>Su-ching, draw blood for crossmatch.</i>

48
00:03:17,458 --> 00:03:18,374
[Su-ching] <i>Yep.</i>

49
00:03:18,375 --> 00:03:19,874
[Cheng-chun] <i>Wen-chih, contact Surgery.</i>

50
00:03:19,875 --> 00:03:21,207
<i>- Say it's urgent.</i>
- [Wen-chih] <i>On it.</i>

51
00:03:21,208 --> 00:03:23,333
- [Cheng-chun] <i>Yuan-ting, intubation.</i>
- [Yuan-ting] <i>Okay.</i>

52
00:03:23,916 --> 00:03:25,000
[sniffles]

53
00:03:29,083 --> 00:03:31,083
[sobbing]

54
00:03:38,416 --> 00:03:40,665
[machines beeping]

55
00:03:40,666 --> 00:03:42,000
Ventilator.

56
00:03:42,583 --> 00:03:44,582
- [EKG beeping]
- [Yuan-ting gasps]

57
00:03:44,583 --> 00:03:47,875
- BP 66 over 49. Heart rate 135.
- [Su-ching] Blood's here.

58
00:03:48,708 --> 00:03:50,874
- Run them wide open. Wen-chih.
- All right.

59
00:03:50,875 --> 00:03:52,957
- Check with Surgery how much longer.
- On it.

60
00:03:52,958 --> 00:03:54,749
[inhales deeply]
Okay, what's her condition?

61
00:03:54,750 --> 00:03:56,832
I just did an echo.
A lot of blood in the abdomen.

62
00:03:56,833 --> 00:03:58,749
- We need a large-bore IV.
- Uh-huh.

63
00:03:58,750 --> 00:04:01,541
- [Yuan-ting] I'll prepare it.
- Doctor, CT results.

64
00:04:02,125 --> 00:04:03,874
- [grunts] Ruptured spleen.
- [Yu-hua sighs]

65
00:04:03,875 --> 00:04:04,958
- Yeah.
- [Wen-chih] Okay.

66
00:04:06,291 --> 00:04:08,665
Surgery want Radiology to perform TAE.

67
00:04:08,666 --> 00:04:10,290
But her BP is too low, they won't do it.

68
00:04:10,291 --> 00:04:12,958
- Who's on shift in Surgery?
- [Wen-chih] Dr. Chuang.

69
00:04:13,541 --> 00:04:14,832
She's hypotensive.

70
00:04:14,833 --> 00:04:17,415
- She can't hold on much longer.
- I know.

71
00:04:17,416 --> 00:04:18,957
[sighs]

72
00:04:18,958 --> 00:04:21,041
[EKG beeping continuously]

73
00:04:23,500 --> 00:04:25,332
[Cheng-chun pants] Dr. Chuang.

74
00:04:25,333 --> 00:04:28,000
A patient with a ruptured spleen
needs emergency surgery.

75
00:04:28,583 --> 00:04:29,957
[Li-te] I know.

76
00:04:29,958 --> 00:04:32,707
Didn't I say to ask Radiology to do TAE?

77
00:04:32,708 --> 00:04:35,165
What's the big deal
about a spleen rupture anyway?

78
00:04:35,166 --> 00:04:36,916
[Cheng-chun] The patient's an R1.

79
00:04:37,791 --> 00:04:38,833
[Li-te] So?

80
00:04:39,500 --> 00:04:43,000
They're still a patient. Doesn't mean
they get to cut in front of mine.

81
00:04:44,208 --> 00:04:45,874
Oh, I just remembered.

82
00:04:45,875 --> 00:04:48,624
Don't you love
performing surgery in the Resus Room?

83
00:04:48,625 --> 00:04:51,208
Why don't you just do it yourself, Doctor?

84
00:04:52,708 --> 00:04:54,332
[Cheng-chun] Because I can't.

85
00:04:54,333 --> 00:04:56,790
You're the only one
who can preserve the spleen.

86
00:04:56,791 --> 00:05:00,332
Dr. Chuang, performing surgery
in the Resus Room was rash of me.

87
00:05:00,333 --> 00:05:02,375
I should have waited. I'm sorry.

88
00:05:03,333 --> 00:05:05,666
[mockingly] Huh?
Sorry, I didn't quite hear you.

89
00:05:06,375 --> 00:05:07,708
[Cheng-chun sighs]

90
00:05:08,333 --> 00:05:10,541
I was wrong. Sorry, Dr. Chuang.

91
00:05:13,458 --> 00:05:15,416
[Li-te] Know your place here, Dr. Chou.

92
00:05:16,791 --> 00:05:19,541
- Call back the team. Now.
- [female doctor] Yes, Doctor.

93
00:05:20,166 --> 00:05:21,166
[Cheng-chun sighs]

94
00:05:24,000 --> 00:05:26,625
[Cheng-chun]
<i>Yu-hua, the OR is ready for her now.</i>

95
00:05:33,500 --> 00:05:35,500
- [EKG beeping]
- [ventilator hissing]

96
00:05:57,208 --> 00:05:58,416
[Geng-ming sighs deeply]

97
00:06:00,916 --> 00:06:02,916
[liquid splattering]

98
00:06:12,875 --> 00:06:14,208
[breath trembling]

99
00:06:16,208 --> 00:06:18,582
[splattering loudly]

100
00:06:18,583 --> 00:06:21,416
- [ominous music playing]
- [Geng-ming breathing shakily]

101
00:06:33,083 --> 00:06:34,665
[music surges]

102
00:06:34,666 --> 00:06:35,582
[music stops]

103
00:06:35,583 --> 00:06:36,665
[Geng-ming exclaims]

104
00:06:36,666 --> 00:06:38,750
[breathing shakily]

105
00:06:41,500 --> 00:06:43,500
- [Geng-ming pants]
- [rhythmic beeping]

106
00:06:44,916 --> 00:06:45,916
[Geng-ming sighs in relief]

107
00:06:47,166 --> 00:06:48,250
[exhales deeply]

108
00:06:51,500 --> 00:06:53,125
Surgery went well.

109
00:06:54,083 --> 00:06:56,000
Why aren't you awake yet?

110
00:06:56,958 --> 00:06:58,875
[breathes shakily]

111
00:07:09,625 --> 00:07:11,416
[breath trembling]

112
00:07:12,500 --> 00:07:14,166
[sobbing softly]

113
00:07:15,416 --> 00:07:17,416
[melancholy music playing]

114
00:07:21,000 --> 00:07:22,000
[Geng-ming sniffles]

115
00:07:29,833 --> 00:07:31,250
- [tray clangs]
- What are you doing?

116
00:07:32,333 --> 00:07:34,083
- [exhales sharply]
- [breathes heavily]

117
00:07:35,666 --> 00:07:37,083
[melancholy music continues]

118
00:07:50,250 --> 00:07:52,666
- [Mrs. Tang and Geng-ming laughing]
- Are you two done yet?

119
00:07:53,958 --> 00:07:54,790
Let's eat.

120
00:07:54,791 --> 00:07:56,625
[inaudible]

121
00:08:14,250 --> 00:08:16,250
[sobbing]

122
00:08:17,416 --> 00:08:18,625
I'm sorry.

123
00:08:23,500 --> 00:08:25,500
[continues sobbing]

124
00:08:28,125 --> 00:08:29,333
I'm sorry.

125
00:08:30,833 --> 00:08:33,041
[breathes heavily]

126
00:08:35,833 --> 00:08:37,957
- [nurse] Yeah, I know.
- [doctor 1] He didn't say anything.

127
00:08:37,958 --> 00:08:39,832
[doctor 2] I wouldn't say it's great news.

128
00:08:39,833 --> 00:08:41,207
[doctor 1] Wait. Hey. Oh.

129
00:08:41,208 --> 00:08:43,124
- [nurse] Hi, Dr. Chou.
- Dr. Chou.

130
00:08:43,125 --> 00:08:44,500
[Chih-cheng] Cheng-chun.

131
00:08:45,250 --> 00:08:47,958
- What's all that about?
- We're screwed, man. Look.

132
00:08:49,375 --> 00:08:51,874
DR. CHENG SHAO-CHING
PROMOTED TO ER DIRECTOR

133
00:08:51,875 --> 00:08:53,874
- [doctor 3] Director Cheng.
- [Shao-ching] Stop.

134
00:08:53,875 --> 00:08:55,290
Thanks. [laughs]

135
00:08:55,291 --> 00:08:57,540
Oh, I'm very flattered. [chuckles]

136
00:08:57,541 --> 00:08:59,374
And thanks for your support.

137
00:08:59,375 --> 00:09:03,082
As of today,
I am the new director of the ER.

138
00:09:03,083 --> 00:09:06,415
As you all know,
my focus has always been research,

139
00:09:06,416 --> 00:09:10,415
and I think the recognition
my papers have received speaks to that.

140
00:09:10,416 --> 00:09:13,124
But it doesn't mean I'll be complacent.

141
00:09:13,125 --> 00:09:16,832
As director,
I'll be the same person I've always been,

142
00:09:16,833 --> 00:09:19,041
someone approachable,

143
00:09:19,625 --> 00:09:20,707
humble,

144
00:09:20,708 --> 00:09:23,582
who takes the time
to mentor those under me.

145
00:09:23,583 --> 00:09:26,291
- Congratulations.
- Ah. Cheers, cheers.

146
00:09:27,458 --> 00:09:29,207
All right, so just hear me out.

147
00:09:29,208 --> 00:09:32,332
Huang You-chang releases his paper
before you get the chance,

148
00:09:32,333 --> 00:09:35,332
so Director Chang
doesn't put in a good word for you and...

149
00:09:35,333 --> 00:09:36,750
Am I missing anything?

150
00:09:37,250 --> 00:09:39,750
WU HSIANG-CHUN: WAITING
CHU KAI-CHIANG: IN CONSULTATION

151
00:09:42,416 --> 00:09:43,707
- Hsiang-chun.
- Yeah?

152
00:09:43,708 --> 00:09:47,040
These critical patients,
why weren't we informed to treat them?

153
00:09:47,041 --> 00:09:48,958
We used to be called right away.

154
00:09:51,125 --> 00:09:52,207
[sighs]

155
00:09:52,208 --> 00:09:56,582
One of the nurses went to Dr. Cheng
earlier to ask about patient allocation,

156
00:09:56,583 --> 00:09:58,374
but he said he was too busy.

157
00:09:58,375 --> 00:10:00,582
Then Hsiu-ju went to raise the issue--

158
00:10:00,583 --> 00:10:03,165
[Hsiu-ju] It's not a nurse's job
to raise an issue.

159
00:10:03,166 --> 00:10:07,583
[sarcastically] Apparently, our job
is just triage and following orders.

160
00:10:08,541 --> 00:10:10,541
Patient allocation

161
00:10:11,166 --> 00:10:14,083
can only be decided
by our noble ER director.

162
00:10:14,833 --> 00:10:16,875
Hsiang-chun, medical cart.

163
00:10:17,458 --> 00:10:18,791
Sure, yep.

164
00:10:21,666 --> 00:10:22,582
Hey.

165
00:10:22,583 --> 00:10:25,249
You see the patients
starting from Li Kuo-chiang.

166
00:10:25,250 --> 00:10:26,916
I'll take the ones before him.

167
00:10:29,000 --> 00:10:30,000
[Geng-ming] Mmm.

168
00:10:31,916 --> 00:10:33,000
You okay?

169
00:10:33,541 --> 00:10:34,791
Tang Hsi will be fine.

170
00:10:42,708 --> 00:10:44,708
[indistinct chatter]

171
00:10:45,541 --> 00:10:46,750
[exhales deeply]

172
00:10:53,666 --> 00:10:55,165
Uh, excuse me?

173
00:10:55,166 --> 00:10:57,082
Did you see where that patient went?

174
00:10:57,083 --> 00:10:58,540
[female patient] No, sorry.

175
00:10:58,541 --> 00:10:59,583
Thank you.

176
00:11:01,375 --> 00:11:03,375
Is there a Li Kuo-chiang here?

177
00:11:04,416 --> 00:11:05,665
Uh, Li Kuo-chiang?

178
00:11:05,666 --> 00:11:07,083
[male patient] No, sorry.

179
00:11:07,666 --> 00:11:08,500
[sighs]

180
00:11:09,375 --> 00:11:10,707
- Hsiang-chun.
- Mmm?

181
00:11:10,708 --> 00:11:12,415
Patient's gone missing.
Can you help find him?

182
00:11:12,416 --> 00:11:14,832
Should I make an announcement?
What's his name?

183
00:11:14,833 --> 00:11:16,416
- Li Kuo-chiang.
- [pa system dings]

184
00:11:17,208 --> 00:11:20,790
[woman over pa system] <i>Code 999.
Male restroom, lobby. Code 999...</i>

185
00:11:20,791 --> 00:11:21,832
First aid kit.

186
00:11:21,833 --> 00:11:23,875
[tense music playing]

187
00:11:24,458 --> 00:11:26,041
[patient groaning]

188
00:11:28,625 --> 00:11:31,582
- [Hsiang-chun] Sir, are you okay?
- [patient] No. [panting]

189
00:11:31,583 --> 00:11:32,707
[heart thumping]

190
00:11:32,708 --> 00:11:34,083
[rapid beeping]

191
00:11:35,375 --> 00:11:36,790
[Hsiang-chun in muffled voice] Dr. Lin!

192
00:11:36,791 --> 00:11:38,874
[patient groaning]

193
00:11:38,875 --> 00:11:40,125
This is Li Kuo-chiang.

194
00:11:41,625 --> 00:11:44,082
- Kuo-chiang. Kuo-chiang.
- Ah, it hurts.

195
00:11:44,083 --> 00:11:45,290
What'd he present with?

196
00:11:45,291 --> 00:11:47,708
Abdominal pain after bumping into a table.

197
00:11:48,291 --> 00:11:49,915
Okay. Get a bed, quickly.

198
00:11:49,916 --> 00:11:51,791
- [groaning]
- [Geng-ming] Where does it hurt?

199
00:11:52,375 --> 00:11:54,375
[Kuo-chiang] It hurts. [cries]

200
00:11:54,958 --> 00:11:55,791
[groans]

201
00:11:56,958 --> 00:11:58,415
[grunts]

202
00:11:58,416 --> 00:12:01,124
- Hsiang-chun, one liter of saline.
- Okay.

203
00:12:01,125 --> 00:12:02,290
[Kuo-chiang grunts] Doctor.

204
00:12:02,291 --> 00:12:05,790
Could you give me something for the pain?
It's unbearable.

205
00:12:05,791 --> 00:12:07,999
- Oh, uh... Hsiang-chun.
- [groaning]

206
00:12:08,000 --> 00:12:09,249
- Give him Ketorolac.
- Yeah? Oh.

207
00:12:09,250 --> 00:12:11,333
[groaning loudly]

208
00:12:14,000 --> 00:12:16,165
[Geng-ming]
Wait. Change to morphine, half dose.

209
00:12:16,166 --> 00:12:18,583
- Okay.
- [Kuo-chiang groaning]

210
00:12:22,875 --> 00:12:24,583
[suspenseful music playing]

211
00:12:25,375 --> 00:12:26,750
[Geng-ming] Won't be long.

212
00:12:27,333 --> 00:12:29,458
[Kuo-chiang continues groaning]

213
00:12:31,916 --> 00:12:33,416
[breathes shakily, groans]

214
00:12:37,000 --> 00:12:38,708
[Hsiang-chun] Hang in there, okay?

215
00:12:40,625 --> 00:12:41,915
Anything show up?

216
00:12:41,916 --> 00:12:43,375
Uh, no.

217
00:12:44,250 --> 00:12:45,082
Nothing?

218
00:12:45,083 --> 00:12:47,499
Send him for a CT.
Could be something else.

219
00:12:47,500 --> 00:12:48,583
Okay.

220
00:12:49,208 --> 00:12:51,208
[Kuo-chiang groans, breathes heavily]

221
00:12:53,208 --> 00:12:54,124
[Geng-ming] <i>Radiology?</i>

222
00:12:54,125 --> 00:12:57,375
We're sending up a patient.
I'd like a CTA of the aorta.

223
00:12:59,083 --> 00:13:01,708
Likely aortic dissection. Right. Thanks.

224
00:13:03,375 --> 00:13:04,458
[sighs]

225
00:13:11,083 --> 00:13:12,083
Come in.

226
00:13:14,041 --> 00:13:16,332
Dr. He. Have a seat.

227
00:13:16,333 --> 00:13:17,458
Oh, I'm fine.

228
00:13:18,041 --> 00:13:19,583
Do you know why I asked you here?

229
00:13:20,166 --> 00:13:22,083
Dr. Cheng, why don't you enlighten me?

230
00:13:22,875 --> 00:13:24,207
In this department,

231
00:13:24,208 --> 00:13:26,708
you're the only attending
who hasn't published a paper.

232
00:13:27,291 --> 00:13:29,332
When can I expect to see one?

233
00:13:29,333 --> 00:13:32,416
[Yu-hua] I think
the current system is deeply flawed.

234
00:13:33,000 --> 00:13:35,499
Should a paper
be the only pathway to promotion?

235
00:13:35,500 --> 00:13:39,665
A doctor's performance is equally,
if not more, important, don't you think?

236
00:13:39,666 --> 00:13:42,749
Dr. He, you started as a resident here.

237
00:13:42,750 --> 00:13:46,250
You know that
the systems are there for a reason.

238
00:13:47,333 --> 00:13:50,415
For example, do you think
a patient can just walk through the door

239
00:13:50,416 --> 00:13:52,624
and see a doctor
without registering first?

240
00:13:52,625 --> 00:13:54,999
Just because
the system's there for a reason

241
00:13:55,000 --> 00:13:56,790
doesn't always mean it works.

242
00:13:56,791 --> 00:13:59,040
If we keep following them
without question,

243
00:13:59,041 --> 00:14:01,208
Yang-Da will never improve.

244
00:14:01,791 --> 00:14:03,832
Well, you're certainly well-spoken.

245
00:14:03,833 --> 00:14:05,624
And your medical skills are good too.

246
00:14:05,625 --> 00:14:07,708
So what I don't get

247
00:14:08,541 --> 00:14:10,666
is why you're being sued by a patient.

248
00:14:13,166 --> 00:14:16,207
The verdict should be out tomorrow, right?

249
00:14:16,208 --> 00:14:20,290
If it's proven that you caused death
through medical negligence,

250
00:14:20,291 --> 00:14:24,582
your performance as a doctor
will deem you unfit for your role.

251
00:14:24,583 --> 00:14:28,707
Without a paper, there's not much
I could do to save your position here.

252
00:14:28,708 --> 00:14:31,249
Maybe you should reconsider

253
00:14:31,250 --> 00:14:33,916
for the sake of Yang-Da's improvement.

254
00:14:35,666 --> 00:14:37,750
LI KUO-CHIANG
LAB AND TEST RESULTS, CT SCAN IMAGES

255
00:14:40,041 --> 00:14:40,875
What's wrong?

256
00:14:41,541 --> 00:14:44,290
Is there a problem with Kuo-chiang's CT?

257
00:14:44,291 --> 00:14:45,583
His CT scan...

258
00:14:47,291 --> 00:14:48,125
It's all clear.

259
00:14:48,708 --> 00:14:51,457
It's all clear? Well, are you sure?

260
00:14:51,458 --> 00:14:54,290
- Should we ask Dr. Chou to take a look?
- [Hsiu-ju] Dr. Lin.

261
00:14:54,291 --> 00:14:56,291
Kuo-chiang said he wants to be discharged.

262
00:14:56,875 --> 00:14:59,000
- Discharged? He can get out of bed?
- [Hsiu-ju] Yeah.

263
00:14:59,583 --> 00:15:00,750
Well, he looks fine to me.

264
00:15:08,250 --> 00:15:09,540
[mouse clicking]

265
00:15:09,541 --> 00:15:12,915
[Geng-ming] Huh?
He had morphine for pain seven days ago.

266
00:15:12,916 --> 00:15:14,416
And again five days ago.

267
00:15:16,041 --> 00:15:17,124
[Kuo-chiang breathing shakily]

268
00:15:17,125 --> 00:15:18,208
Hey!

269
00:15:24,833 --> 00:15:25,666
[Hsiu-ju] Hmm.

270
00:15:26,541 --> 00:15:28,750
- Another scammer.
- [sighs heavily]

271
00:15:30,791 --> 00:15:32,041
[exhales softly]

272
00:15:35,208 --> 00:15:37,208
[siren blaring distantly]

273
00:15:41,958 --> 00:15:43,750
[soft piano music playing]

274
00:15:44,500 --> 00:15:45,625
[Geng-ming] I'm sorry.

275
00:15:46,333 --> 00:15:47,708
I can't do anything right.

276
00:15:53,875 --> 00:15:55,124
Oh.

277
00:15:55,125 --> 00:15:57,291
- [Mrs. Tang breathes heavily]
- [Geng-ming] Mrs. Tang.

278
00:15:58,333 --> 00:15:59,166
Uh...

279
00:15:59,958 --> 00:16:00,915
[Mrs. Tang shudders]

280
00:16:00,916 --> 00:16:03,625
[Geng-ming] We didn't want to alarm you
until she was stable.

281
00:16:05,708 --> 00:16:07,708
[Mrs. Tang crying softly]

282
00:16:17,666 --> 00:16:19,666
[continues crying softly]

283
00:16:24,041 --> 00:16:27,290
Oh, my darling. Wake up, sweetheart.

284
00:16:27,291 --> 00:16:29,375
[sobbing softly]

285
00:16:32,666 --> 00:16:35,083
Didn't you promise you'd take care of me?

286
00:16:35,833 --> 00:16:38,666
[sobs] This wasn't part of the plan.

287
00:16:39,791 --> 00:16:43,000
It's not supposed to be you
lying there. [sobs]

288
00:16:45,083 --> 00:16:48,000
Rest for now, but wake up soon, okay?

289
00:16:48,791 --> 00:16:50,083
I need you.

290
00:16:51,041 --> 00:16:53,041
[sobs] Do you hear me?

291
00:16:54,958 --> 00:16:56,958
[sobbing loudly]

292
00:17:01,208 --> 00:17:03,707
[continues sobbing]

293
00:17:03,708 --> 00:17:05,957
[indistinct chatter]

294
00:17:05,958 --> 00:17:07,999
Let me know if his pain gets any worse.

295
00:17:08,000 --> 00:17:09,040
- I will.
- Thanks.

296
00:17:09,041 --> 00:17:11,457
- No problem.
- [Yuan-ting] Dr. Lin. New patient.

297
00:17:11,458 --> 00:17:15,207
- Can you tell me where it hurts?
- [patient groaning] I'm in so much pain.

298
00:17:15,208 --> 00:17:16,832
- [Yuan-ting] How did this happen?
- [sighs]

299
00:17:16,833 --> 00:17:19,749
I just got hit by a car.
I think my arm's dislocated.

300
00:17:19,750 --> 00:17:23,000
- Can you get me something strong? Like--
- [Geng-ming] Like morphine?

301
00:17:26,625 --> 00:17:28,290
I was concerned about you yesterday.

302
00:17:28,291 --> 00:17:31,124
I kept trying to find a reason
you were in so much pain.

303
00:17:31,125 --> 00:17:33,499
But Doctor,
I was really just hit by a car.

304
00:17:33,500 --> 00:17:34,625
Are you injured or not?

305
00:17:36,166 --> 00:17:37,166
[sighs]

306
00:17:39,000 --> 00:17:40,625
[both sigh]

307
00:17:43,416 --> 00:17:45,249
X-ray and discharge him
if nothing shows up.

308
00:17:45,250 --> 00:17:46,624
- [nurse] Yes, Doctor.
- Please.

309
00:17:46,625 --> 00:17:47,999
I won't let you scam us again.

310
00:17:48,000 --> 00:17:51,083
Doctor, I... [breathing heavily]

311
00:17:52,000 --> 00:17:53,457
[machines beeping]

312
00:17:53,458 --> 00:17:55,124
[Geng-ming]
After that, he'll be good to go.

313
00:17:55,125 --> 00:17:56,666
- Thank you, Doctor.
- Okay.

314
00:17:58,041 --> 00:17:59,165
[Hsiang-chun] Dr. Lin.

315
00:17:59,166 --> 00:18:00,415
Kuo-chiang's gone again.

316
00:18:00,416 --> 00:18:03,290
Yuan-ting took him for an X-ray,
and he never came back.

317
00:18:03,291 --> 00:18:05,374
- We looked everywhere.
- [Geng-ming inhales deeply]

318
00:18:05,375 --> 00:18:07,457
- I'll report a self-discharge.
- Okay.

319
00:18:07,458 --> 00:18:09,582
- If he shows up again, let me know, okay?
- Mmm-hmm.

320
00:18:09,583 --> 00:18:11,541
- No more scamming.
- Okay.

321
00:18:12,291 --> 00:18:13,624
[Hsiu-ju] I knew it!

322
00:18:13,625 --> 00:18:15,249
- [screaming]
- [Yu-hua exclaims]

323
00:18:15,250 --> 00:18:17,082
- I knew it!
- [Wen-chih] What's going on?

324
00:18:17,083 --> 00:18:19,207
- Hey.
- [sighs] The verdict was announced.

325
00:18:19,208 --> 00:18:22,124
- No medical negligence!
- [all cheering]

326
00:18:22,125 --> 00:18:24,374
[Wen-chih] Yeah! Yes!

327
00:18:24,375 --> 00:18:26,790
- [Hsiang-chun] Yes!
- [Wen-chih] Congratulations!

328
00:18:26,791 --> 00:18:28,082
[Wen-chih laughs]

329
00:18:28,083 --> 00:18:31,124
[nurses chanting] Yu-hua! Yu-hua! Yu-hua!

330
00:18:31,125 --> 00:18:34,332
Yu-hua! Yu-hua! Yu-hua! Yu-hua! Yu-hua!

331
00:18:34,333 --> 00:18:37,707
Yu-hua! Yu-hua! Yu-hua! Yu-hua!

332
00:18:37,708 --> 00:18:41,624
[man] Yang-Da Hospital killed my sister!
They have no conscience!

333
00:18:41,625 --> 00:18:43,624
All they do is dodge responsibility.

334
00:18:43,625 --> 00:18:46,540
- [woman] The hospital killed her.
- [man] This hospital is a disgrace!

335
00:18:46,541 --> 00:18:49,124
- How many more patients have you killed...
- Sir, calm down.

336
00:18:49,125 --> 00:18:51,207
- [clamoring]
- My sister's blood is on your hands!

337
00:18:51,208 --> 00:18:53,707
- [security] If you don't stop...
- [man] You never apologized.

338
00:18:53,708 --> 00:18:55,582
- You even said you did your best.
- Calm down. Stop.

339
00:18:55,583 --> 00:18:57,915
- Please stop.
- Your fucking best! What a joke.

340
00:18:57,916 --> 00:19:02,332
This woman's name is Lin Yu-chuan.
And Yang-Da Hospital killed her!

341
00:19:02,333 --> 00:19:04,499
- Where's the justice for my sister?
- Sir, calm down.

342
00:19:04,500 --> 00:19:05,957
They failed her!

343
00:19:05,958 --> 00:19:08,457
- Mr. Lin.
- That's the killer right there.

344
00:19:08,458 --> 00:19:11,582
She died because of you.
And you still get to work here?

345
00:19:11,583 --> 00:19:14,915
This is Dr. He Yu-hua. Remember her name.

346
00:19:14,916 --> 00:19:16,749
- No filming, please.
- Remember her face.

347
00:19:16,750 --> 00:19:19,457
- Stay as far away from her as you can.
- [Hsiang-chun] No filming.

348
00:19:19,458 --> 00:19:21,082
[Mr. Lin]
Otherwise, you might end up dead.

349
00:19:21,083 --> 00:19:24,708
- [security] Enough. You need to leave now.
- [Mr. Lin] We want justice for Yu-chuan!

350
00:19:25,583 --> 00:19:26,874
Mr. Yu, I...

351
00:19:26,875 --> 00:19:28,916
[menacing music playing]

352
00:19:29,916 --> 00:19:31,999
[all scream]

353
00:19:32,000 --> 00:19:33,750
Hey! Ching-hsiang, what are you doing?

354
00:19:34,333 --> 00:19:35,666
[Hsiang-chun] Call the police!

355
00:19:36,541 --> 00:19:37,749
Mr. Yu.

356
00:19:37,750 --> 00:19:39,249
- [woman whimpers]
- What are you doing?

357
00:19:39,250 --> 00:19:41,832
- [woman] Put it down! Don't do this!
- Mr. Yu, stop this.

358
00:19:41,833 --> 00:19:44,124
- Don't do anything stupid.
- [Ching-hsiang panting]

359
00:19:44,125 --> 00:19:45,957
He Yu-hua!

360
00:19:45,958 --> 00:19:47,249
- [screams]
- Mr. Yu...

361
00:19:47,250 --> 00:19:48,208
[both scream]

362
00:19:48,708 --> 00:19:50,415
- [blade whooshes]
- [all scream]

363
00:19:50,416 --> 00:19:52,207
[Cheng-chun grunts, strains]

364
00:19:52,208 --> 00:19:53,875
[screams] Get off me!

365
00:19:54,458 --> 00:19:55,540
Get off me!

366
00:19:55,541 --> 00:19:58,457
[yelling] Get lost!
I'll kill you! I'll kill you all!

367
00:19:58,458 --> 00:20:00,166
- Stay back! Stay back!
- [Hsiu-ju screams]

368
00:20:01,583 --> 00:20:04,499
Come any closer, I'll kill you!
I'll kill you all!

369
00:20:04,500 --> 00:20:07,583
- [screams]
- [breathing heavily]

370
00:20:09,916 --> 00:20:11,957
- This is what you deserve!
- [people scream]

371
00:20:11,958 --> 00:20:13,040
[screams]

372
00:20:13,041 --> 00:20:16,541
- [squelches]
- [Yu-hua breathing shakily]

373
00:20:19,875 --> 00:20:20,707
Cheng-chun.

374
00:20:20,708 --> 00:20:22,290
- [squelching]
- [breathing heavily]

375
00:20:22,291 --> 00:20:23,374
[Ching-hsiang] Let go!

376
00:20:23,375 --> 00:20:25,749
I said, let go! Let go!

377
00:20:25,750 --> 00:20:27,749
- [grunts loudly]
- [Ching-hsiang groans]

378
00:20:27,750 --> 00:20:29,041
[yelps]

379
00:20:29,625 --> 00:20:31,457
- [all grunting]
- [Wen-chih] Stay there!

380
00:20:31,458 --> 00:20:33,040
- [security] Calm down!
- Cheng-chun.

381
00:20:33,041 --> 00:20:35,457
- [Ching-hsiang] Get off me. Get off me!
- [all groaning]

382
00:20:35,458 --> 00:20:37,957
- [Ching-hsiang screams]
- [Chih-cheng] Wen-chih, come on!

383
00:20:37,958 --> 00:20:40,125
- I'll kill you! I'll kill you all!
- [all screaming]

384
00:20:41,208 --> 00:20:42,041
[Yu-hua gasps]

385
00:20:43,041 --> 00:20:44,499
[liquid sloshing]

386
00:20:44,500 --> 00:20:47,040
[security] Stay back. Don't go any closer.

387
00:20:47,041 --> 00:20:49,040
- [screams]
- [Mr. Lin] My sister wouldn't want this.

388
00:20:49,041 --> 00:20:50,999
Please, Ching-hsiang!

389
00:20:51,000 --> 00:20:53,415
- Stay back! Stay back!
- [people scream]

390
00:20:53,416 --> 00:20:56,124
- Stay back.
- Ching-hsiang, we can still appeal.

391
00:20:56,125 --> 00:20:58,290
[yelling] Appeal?
What's the use of an appeal?

392
00:20:58,291 --> 00:21:00,665
They couldn't care less
if people like us live or die.

393
00:21:00,666 --> 00:21:03,124
No matter how many times we appeal,

394
00:21:03,125 --> 00:21:06,499
the hospital and the doctors,
they're never wrong, right?

395
00:21:06,500 --> 00:21:08,790
[sarcastically]
They're just doing a great job!

396
00:21:08,791 --> 00:21:12,165
Did my wife and child deserve to die?

397
00:21:12,166 --> 00:21:15,874
No! No! I won't accept it!
I'll never accept it!

398
00:21:15,875 --> 00:21:17,749
[menacing music builds]

399
00:21:17,750 --> 00:21:18,665
Yu-hua.

400
00:21:18,666 --> 00:21:19,874
What are you doing?

401
00:21:19,875 --> 00:21:22,541
Don't come any closer.
I'll light this place up!

402
00:21:23,208 --> 00:21:25,208
[high-pitched ringing]

403
00:21:30,625 --> 00:21:32,625
[ringing continues]

404
00:21:35,416 --> 00:21:36,541
[inaudible]

405
00:21:39,916 --> 00:21:41,750
[inaudible]

406
00:21:45,541 --> 00:21:47,332
[ringing fades]

407
00:21:47,333 --> 00:21:48,250
[lighter thuds]

408
00:21:50,125 --> 00:21:52,125
[melancholy music playing]

409
00:21:57,375 --> 00:21:58,500
[security] Get down!

410
00:22:00,416 --> 00:22:01,833
[Ching-hsiang choking]

411
00:22:04,916 --> 00:22:06,458
[choking]

412
00:22:13,333 --> 00:22:15,207
Organophosphate. Poison's kicked in.

413
00:22:15,208 --> 00:22:16,916
Flip him on his back. Quick.

414
00:22:20,125 --> 00:22:22,499
Do NG irrigation first
and inject atropine.

415
00:22:22,500 --> 00:22:24,166
- [Wen-chih] Yeah, oaky.
- Got it.

416
00:22:27,125 --> 00:22:28,875
I'm not gonna let you die.

417
00:22:38,458 --> 00:22:40,708
[indistinct chatter]

418
00:22:43,541 --> 00:22:46,875
You shouldn't have stepped in like that.
What if he really lit it?

419
00:22:48,083 --> 00:22:49,415
Do you hear yourself?

420
00:22:49,416 --> 00:22:51,790
Or did you forget about your hand?

421
00:22:51,791 --> 00:22:54,582
You just grabbed the knife
without thinking.

422
00:22:54,583 --> 00:22:56,290
What if the nerves are damaged?

423
00:22:56,291 --> 00:22:57,707
[scoffs]

424
00:22:57,708 --> 00:23:00,958
I only thought about you being okay.

425
00:23:02,083 --> 00:23:03,916
[sentimental music playing]

426
00:23:06,791 --> 00:23:07,625
[inhales deeply]

427
00:23:08,916 --> 00:23:09,750
[Wen-chih] Dr. He?

428
00:23:10,833 --> 00:23:12,875
Uh, Yu Ching-hsiang, he's awake now.

429
00:23:16,166 --> 00:23:18,166
[EKG beeping faintly]

430
00:23:24,291 --> 00:23:26,957
[Yu-hua] <i>If you hadn't have
drunk so much that night</i>

431
00:23:26,958 --> 00:23:29,333
and brought your wife to the ER sooner,

432
00:23:30,583 --> 00:23:32,208
everything would've been different.

433
00:23:34,916 --> 00:23:36,916
[soft piano music playing]

434
00:23:45,750 --> 00:23:46,750
[sighs softly]

435
00:23:47,875 --> 00:23:49,916
Why did you save me?

436
00:23:50,875 --> 00:23:53,916
I know that you got a promotion
that day at your work.

437
00:23:54,500 --> 00:23:57,250
- So you went to dinner to celebrate.
- [exhales shakily]

438
00:23:58,583 --> 00:24:00,415
Your wife told me.

439
00:24:00,416 --> 00:24:04,000
[breathing shakily] I've never seen
my husband this happy before.

440
00:24:05,041 --> 00:24:09,000
[Yu-hua] That day, you even came up
with a name for the baby together

441
00:24:09,791 --> 00:24:12,541
and talked about
all your plans for the future.

442
00:24:14,625 --> 00:24:17,583
[Yu-chuan] <i>I didn't tell him
that I wasn't feeling well.</i>

443
00:24:18,375 --> 00:24:21,374
Until... [breathes shakily]
his dinner was over.

444
00:24:21,375 --> 00:24:23,082
When he got home,

445
00:24:23,083 --> 00:24:26,250
he saw I was in pain
and drove here so fast.

446
00:24:27,000 --> 00:24:31,333
Please don't tell the police.
He drove drunk. Please.

447
00:24:32,041 --> 00:24:33,416
We're so excited

448
00:24:34,041 --> 00:24:36,040
to finally meet our baby.

449
00:24:36,041 --> 00:24:38,125
[breathing shakily]

450
00:24:40,958 --> 00:24:42,583
[breath trembling]

451
00:24:45,166 --> 00:24:47,750
She was thinking of you
in her last moments.

452
00:24:48,625 --> 00:24:50,749
Live well for her.

453
00:24:50,750 --> 00:24:53,125
And if you meet again in the next life,

454
00:24:54,541 --> 00:24:55,790
take care of each other.

455
00:24:55,791 --> 00:24:57,875
[crying]

456
00:25:01,208 --> 00:25:02,625
[sobbing]

457
00:25:08,791 --> 00:25:10,416
[Ching-hsiang wailing]

458
00:25:21,583 --> 00:25:22,916
[Geng-ming sighs]

459
00:25:23,750 --> 00:25:24,750
You okay?

460
00:25:29,250 --> 00:25:30,082
I'm sorry.

461
00:25:30,083 --> 00:25:33,958
My client's behavior
put everyone in danger.

462
00:25:35,708 --> 00:25:37,250
[breathes deeply]

463
00:25:37,833 --> 00:25:39,583
I understand how you feel.

464
00:25:42,041 --> 00:25:43,875
After so much effort,

465
00:25:45,041 --> 00:25:46,500
you didn't get a good result.

466
00:25:50,666 --> 00:25:51,791
But you did your best.

467
00:25:52,375 --> 00:25:53,375
Right?

468
00:25:55,416 --> 00:25:57,416
[sentimental music playing]

469
00:26:02,583 --> 00:26:03,916
[laughs softly]

470
00:26:07,166 --> 00:26:08,791
You were a rookie when I met you.

471
00:26:09,541 --> 00:26:12,041
Now you seem like a real doctor.

472
00:26:13,500 --> 00:26:15,833
[exhales deeply] Hmm.

473
00:26:20,000 --> 00:26:23,124
If we see each other again,
let's be friends, okay?

474
00:26:23,125 --> 00:26:24,041
Geng-ming.

475
00:26:33,250 --> 00:26:34,832
[sighs]

476
00:26:34,833 --> 00:26:36,415
[indistinct chatter]

477
00:26:36,416 --> 00:26:37,749
[winces]

478
00:26:37,750 --> 00:26:39,457
- Cheng-chun.
- Mmm?

479
00:26:39,458 --> 00:26:40,665
Is your hand okay?

480
00:26:40,666 --> 00:26:43,249
Ah... It's fine, nothing serious.

481
00:26:43,250 --> 00:26:46,875
If you wanted to press charges
against Mr. Yu, I can help you.

482
00:26:47,458 --> 00:26:48,582
[exhales sharply]

483
00:26:48,583 --> 00:26:50,666
[Chia-hsin] Cheng-chun,
can I ask you something?

484
00:26:52,125 --> 00:26:53,541
[nurse] Patient incoming.

485
00:26:54,500 --> 00:26:55,583
Let's talk later.

486
00:26:59,166 --> 00:27:01,040
- How'd he get injured?
- [EMT] Ran out into the road.

487
00:27:01,041 --> 00:27:03,249
The driver couldn't brake in time
and hit him.

488
00:27:03,250 --> 00:27:04,999
[EKG beeping]

489
00:27:05,000 --> 00:27:06,333
Li Kuo-chiang?

490
00:27:07,125 --> 00:27:08,207
You know him?

491
00:27:08,208 --> 00:27:11,124
He was trying to scam morphine.
I drove him away.

492
00:27:11,125 --> 00:27:12,582
[EKG beeping rapidly]

493
00:27:12,583 --> 00:27:14,457
- Asystole.
- Take over.

494
00:27:14,458 --> 00:27:15,790
Geng-ming, intubate.

495
00:27:15,791 --> 00:27:17,333
[Su-ching] Prepping now.

496
00:27:18,791 --> 00:27:19,915
[Wen-chih panting]

497
00:27:19,916 --> 00:27:21,750
[tense music playing]

498
00:27:26,291 --> 00:27:27,875
[breathing shakily]

499
00:27:35,958 --> 00:27:36,958
[tires screech]

500
00:27:37,750 --> 00:27:39,708
[Su-ching in muffled voice]
Ready for intubation.

501
00:27:40,333 --> 00:27:42,041
[muffled clanging]

502
00:27:46,041 --> 00:27:46,957
[muffled] Dr. Lin.

503
00:27:46,958 --> 00:27:48,707
[clear] Dr. Lin!

504
00:27:48,708 --> 00:27:50,290
[panting]

505
00:27:50,291 --> 00:27:52,124
What's going on? Do it now.

506
00:27:52,125 --> 00:27:54,208
[breathing heavily]

507
00:27:54,791 --> 00:27:56,208
[tuts] Out of the way.

508
00:27:58,125 --> 00:27:59,125
Hold compressions.

509
00:28:00,583 --> 00:28:01,915
Tube.

510
00:28:01,916 --> 00:28:03,208
Bag him.

511
00:28:04,000 --> 00:28:07,249
Okay. Okay.

512
00:28:07,250 --> 00:28:09,125
Good. Resume compressions.

513
00:28:11,875 --> 00:28:13,541
[Su-ching] Securing at 22 centimeters.

514
00:28:15,791 --> 00:28:17,958
Don't stand there. Take over compressions.

515
00:28:19,083 --> 00:28:21,665
- Wen-chih. Epi, one every three minutes.
- [Wen-chih] Two.

516
00:28:21,666 --> 00:28:23,124
One. Switch.

517
00:28:23,125 --> 00:28:24,666
[panting]

518
00:28:26,208 --> 00:28:27,208
Ventilator.

519
00:28:28,041 --> 00:28:29,750
[Geng-ming panting]

520
00:28:31,250 --> 00:28:33,250
[suspenseful music playing]

521
00:28:37,500 --> 00:28:39,583
[heart thumping]

522
00:28:48,458 --> 00:28:50,458
[Wen-chih in muffled voice]
Epi 1 milligram, IV push.

523
00:28:52,833 --> 00:28:53,833
Done.

524
00:28:58,541 --> 00:29:00,541
[panting]

525
00:29:02,041 --> 00:29:03,665
[Yu-hua] <i>A man's life is in your hands.</i>

526
00:29:03,666 --> 00:29:05,707
[Chien-te] <i>My dad's unconscious.
If anything happens...</i>

527
00:29:05,708 --> 00:29:07,582
[Cheng-chun]
<i>If you can't handle a minor setback,</i>

528
00:29:07,583 --> 00:29:10,165
<i>- hand in your resignation.</i>
- [woman] <i>Stop pretending it's okay.</i>

529
00:29:10,166 --> 00:29:12,750
<i>Chia-hao wouldn't be like this
if it wasn't for you.</i>

530
00:29:14,458 --> 00:29:16,458
[panting]

531
00:29:17,750 --> 00:29:19,625
[somber music playing]

532
00:29:27,541 --> 00:29:29,541
[panting]

533
00:29:32,041 --> 00:29:32,875
[EKG flatlining]

534
00:29:36,791 --> 00:29:38,125
[Geng-ming panting]

535
00:29:42,416 --> 00:29:44,750
That's enough. It's been 30 minutes.

536
00:29:49,750 --> 00:29:51,124
[Geng-ming whimpers]

537
00:29:51,125 --> 00:29:52,500
[EKG flatlining]

538
00:29:56,291 --> 00:29:59,290
Time of death, 17:41. Notify the morgue.

539
00:29:59,291 --> 00:30:00,749
[Wen-chih] Okay.

540
00:30:00,750 --> 00:30:02,833
[breathing heavily]

541
00:30:03,791 --> 00:30:06,916
[Wen-chih] This is Resus Room 1.
We have a deceased patient.

542
00:30:10,541 --> 00:30:12,541
[Geng-ming panting]

543
00:30:14,791 --> 00:30:18,291
[Pi-tan slurring] Do you know
who the best doctor here is?

544
00:30:18,875 --> 00:30:20,165
[nurses] Uh...

545
00:30:20,166 --> 00:30:22,124
Lin Geng-ming.

546
00:30:22,125 --> 00:30:23,665
- [nurse 1] Oh.
- [nurse 2 chuckles]

547
00:30:23,666 --> 00:30:26,708
Ah! Here he is right now.

548
00:30:27,708 --> 00:30:28,540
You've been drinking.

549
00:30:28,541 --> 00:30:31,999
Oh, basically nothing. Just a little bit.

550
00:30:32,000 --> 00:30:33,083
[sighs]

551
00:30:34,041 --> 00:30:37,374
I could tell you're drunk.
And looking for a bed.

552
00:30:37,375 --> 00:30:39,374
I should've known you wouldn't change.

553
00:30:39,375 --> 00:30:42,749
[spluttering]
No, I won't drink again after today.

554
00:30:42,750 --> 00:30:46,457
I just came to tell you something.
I'm just happy because--

555
00:30:46,458 --> 00:30:47,375
Whoa...

556
00:30:49,125 --> 00:30:50,915
You and I aren't friends.

557
00:30:50,916 --> 00:30:52,582
[somber music playing]

558
00:30:52,583 --> 00:30:54,250
If you're not here for treatment, get out.

559
00:30:54,833 --> 00:30:59,083
Oh... Dr. Lin. [laughs] You're such a joker.

560
00:30:59,666 --> 00:31:00,915
We're buddies, remember?

561
00:31:00,916 --> 00:31:02,457
[Pi-tan groans]

562
00:31:02,458 --> 00:31:03,749
I'm not joking.

563
00:31:03,750 --> 00:31:04,916
[exhales sharply]

564
00:31:08,958 --> 00:31:10,708
I don't want to see your face again.

565
00:31:11,500 --> 00:31:12,791
You're not welcome here.

566
00:31:13,375 --> 00:31:15,458
[breathing heavily]

567
00:31:19,458 --> 00:31:20,624
Let's go.

568
00:31:20,625 --> 00:31:23,250
[breath trembling]

569
00:31:30,125 --> 00:31:31,750
[vending machine thuds]

570
00:31:35,708 --> 00:31:37,333
[Cheng-chun chuckles softly]

571
00:31:42,375 --> 00:31:44,375
Li Kuo-chiang's death isn't your fault.

572
00:31:45,208 --> 00:31:46,291
He was an adult.

573
00:31:46,875 --> 00:31:48,833
Responsible for his own actions.

574
00:31:51,541 --> 00:31:53,374
Tang Hsi wasn't your fault either.

575
00:31:53,375 --> 00:31:55,333
[breathes shakily]

576
00:32:00,208 --> 00:32:03,624
[crying softly] I wasn't able to help
Tang Hsi or Kuo-chiang.

577
00:32:03,625 --> 00:32:05,458
I'm not qualified to be a doctor.

578
00:32:06,875 --> 00:32:10,166
[inhales deeply]
You know, every doctor feels like that.

579
00:32:10,750 --> 00:32:11,750
At some point.

580
00:32:13,500 --> 00:32:15,541
But having feelings isn't a weakness.

581
00:32:17,833 --> 00:32:20,666
Do you know the reason that I hired you?

582
00:32:23,625 --> 00:32:26,624
On the day of the interviews,
when it was almost your turn,

583
00:32:26,625 --> 00:32:27,791
where'd you go?

584
00:32:28,875 --> 00:32:30,374
[soft music playing]

585
00:32:30,375 --> 00:32:32,458
[distant shuffling]

586
00:32:37,833 --> 00:32:39,999
We have some excellent candidates
this year.

587
00:32:40,000 --> 00:32:41,874
Yeah, they always keep getting better.

588
00:32:41,875 --> 00:32:44,041
[patient groaning]

589
00:32:46,458 --> 00:32:48,457
[doctor] Interviewees, please stay put.

590
00:32:48,458 --> 00:32:51,124
We'll call you in shortly
in numerical order.

591
00:32:51,125 --> 00:32:52,957
[groaning]

592
00:32:52,958 --> 00:32:54,125
CHECK-IN NUMBER 3

593
00:32:55,083 --> 00:32:57,041
Oh, oh. No, no! [panting]

594
00:32:57,791 --> 00:33:00,125
- Sir, sir, don't do that. Don't do...
- [patient groaning]

595
00:33:01,291 --> 00:33:03,207
Sir, don't do that. Let me help, okay?

596
00:33:03,208 --> 00:33:04,624
[doctor] Number 1, come through now...

597
00:33:04,625 --> 00:33:07,207
[Cheng-chun] <i>There were dozens
of high-achieving graduates that day.</i>

598
00:33:07,208 --> 00:33:08,874
I'll take you to a doctor. This way.

599
00:33:08,875 --> 00:33:11,750
[Cheng-chun] <i>But you were the only one
who stood up and helped that man.</i>

600
00:33:12,333 --> 00:33:14,415
<i>You saw the risks and acted fast.</i>

601
00:33:14,416 --> 00:33:16,625
Not many people would've done that.

602
00:33:17,208 --> 00:33:20,083
This hospital needs a doctor like you.

603
00:33:23,291 --> 00:33:25,625
[inhales deeply] Do you remember

604
00:33:26,666 --> 00:33:29,583
what you said
to the last question I asked you?

605
00:33:31,833 --> 00:33:34,833
You barely passed the written exam,
and you were late today.

606
00:33:35,833 --> 00:33:38,500
I'd like to know
why you want to be an emergency physician.

607
00:33:40,291 --> 00:33:41,290
Because...

608
00:33:41,291 --> 00:33:42,875
[soft music continues]

609
00:33:49,583 --> 00:33:50,666
[sniffles]

610
00:33:52,166 --> 00:33:53,250
Because...

611
00:33:56,708 --> 00:33:58,208
[loudly] I want to save lives.

612
00:34:00,750 --> 00:34:02,250
[breathes deeply]

613
00:34:06,125 --> 00:34:07,125
[sniffles]

614
00:34:09,125 --> 00:34:10,791
"Because I want to save lives."

615
00:34:11,875 --> 00:34:13,874
[sobbing]

616
00:34:13,875 --> 00:34:15,375
I want to save lives.

617
00:34:16,708 --> 00:34:17,708
Uh-huh.

618
00:34:19,041 --> 00:34:20,458
Come back when you're ready.

619
00:34:21,333 --> 00:34:22,708
With your head held high.

620
00:34:25,958 --> 00:34:27,583
[sniffles]

621
00:34:28,666 --> 00:34:30,666
[breathing shakily]

622
00:34:36,625 --> 00:34:38,625
[sobbing]

623
00:34:54,875 --> 00:34:56,208
[winces]

624
00:35:02,250 --> 00:35:04,207
So how's your hand?

625
00:35:04,208 --> 00:35:05,457
Much better.

626
00:35:05,458 --> 00:35:08,041
A very skilled doctor
stitched me right up.

627
00:35:11,583 --> 00:35:12,791
You chat with Geng-ming?

628
00:35:13,875 --> 00:35:15,958
He'll be okay. I believe in him.

629
00:35:18,958 --> 00:35:21,083
I met with You-chang yesterday.

630
00:35:26,291 --> 00:35:28,625
[You-chang]
Where would you like to eat? My treat.

631
00:35:29,833 --> 00:35:31,207
- [Yu-hua sighs]
- [You-chang exhales]

632
00:35:31,208 --> 00:35:33,000
Tang Hsi's mom is your patient, right?

633
00:35:35,000 --> 00:35:35,999
She is.

634
00:35:36,000 --> 00:35:37,874
And how has she been doing?

635
00:35:37,875 --> 00:35:41,832
Uh, for a patient with stage 4 cancer,
she's okay. Mmm.

636
00:35:41,833 --> 00:35:44,333
I saw her latest scan.

637
00:35:45,875 --> 00:35:47,874
You know how treatment works,
it's a process.

638
00:35:47,875 --> 00:35:50,665
I believe the next CT scan
will show improvement.

639
00:35:50,666 --> 00:35:52,290
[Yu-hua] How can you be so sure?

640
00:35:52,291 --> 00:35:55,540
When you treat something the right way,
it'll lead to good results.

641
00:35:55,541 --> 00:35:58,207
- What if there's not a good result?
- [laughs] Yu-hua, you're a doctor.

642
00:35:58,208 --> 00:36:01,040
Surely you understand that medications
can affect people differently.

643
00:36:01,041 --> 00:36:02,082
There's no cure-all drug.

644
00:36:02,083 --> 00:36:03,374
Then is it the truth

645
00:36:03,375 --> 00:36:06,540
when you say that treating something
the right way will lead to good results?

646
00:36:06,541 --> 00:36:08,124
Well, now you're twisting my words.

647
00:36:08,125 --> 00:36:09,832
[Yu-hua] Tang Hsi is still in the ICU.

648
00:36:09,833 --> 00:36:13,957
And I just want to know if I can help
her mother because she can't right now.

649
00:36:13,958 --> 00:36:16,000
Please. Tell me the truth.

650
00:36:17,125 --> 00:36:19,374
Is the drug effective or not?

651
00:36:19,375 --> 00:36:21,166
[tense music playing]

652
00:36:22,083 --> 00:36:23,708
<i>I can't trust You-chang anymore.</i>

653
00:36:24,875 --> 00:36:27,290
So I really hope that
you can finish your paper.

654
00:36:27,291 --> 00:36:30,208
The research into the drug
needs to be solid.

655
00:36:32,083 --> 00:36:35,374
[sighs] No pressure then.
I'll try not to disappoint you.

656
00:36:35,375 --> 00:36:37,000
[chuckles]

657
00:36:38,583 --> 00:36:40,790
[Geng-ming panting]

658
00:36:40,791 --> 00:36:42,832
[indistinct announcement over pa system]

659
00:36:42,833 --> 00:36:43,916
[Geng-ming] Excuse me.

660
00:36:46,333 --> 00:36:48,000
[panting]

661
00:36:51,458 --> 00:36:52,666
How are you feeling?

662
00:36:54,791 --> 00:36:56,083
[weakly] Hungry.

663
00:36:56,666 --> 00:36:57,833
[exhales deeply]

664
00:37:02,833 --> 00:37:04,041
I'm sorry.

665
00:37:06,041 --> 00:37:07,833
[breath trembling]

666
00:37:08,458 --> 00:37:11,666
When it happened, I couldn't do anything.
I'm sorry.

667
00:37:13,000 --> 00:37:14,125
[weakly] It's fine.

668
00:37:16,208 --> 00:37:17,250
Thanks...

669
00:37:19,541 --> 00:37:21,707
for always being there for me.

670
00:37:21,708 --> 00:37:23,791
[mellow music playing]

671
00:37:27,041 --> 00:37:29,041
[crying softly]

672
00:37:35,041 --> 00:37:37,041
[Geng-ming breathes heavily]

673
00:37:41,750 --> 00:37:42,958
[Geng-ming sighs]

674
00:37:45,583 --> 00:37:46,958
I'm glad you're okay.

675
00:37:51,333 --> 00:37:52,166
[knock on door]

676
00:37:53,291 --> 00:37:54,708
[clears throat] Come in.

677
00:37:59,875 --> 00:38:00,874
[grunts]

678
00:38:00,875 --> 00:38:07,041
BETEL NUTS

679
00:38:09,541 --> 00:38:10,541
[coins jingling]

680
00:38:14,125 --> 00:38:16,416
[suspenseful music playing]

681
00:38:24,750 --> 00:38:25,583
[sniffs]

682
00:38:26,500 --> 00:38:27,332
[gulps]

683
00:38:27,333 --> 00:38:30,500
- Yeah, I tried calling him a few times.
- Okay, yeah. Hey, Doc.

684
00:38:31,083 --> 00:38:32,333
Have you seen Pi-tan?

685
00:38:33,000 --> 00:38:33,915
What's the matter?

686
00:38:33,916 --> 00:38:36,374
[man] Well, he got a new job,
so he treated us to a meal.

687
00:38:36,375 --> 00:38:38,540
And then he left dinner to come here
and never came back.

688
00:38:38,541 --> 00:38:40,707
Wait. You say that he found a new job?

689
00:38:40,708 --> 00:38:41,791
[man] Yeah.

690
00:38:44,333 --> 00:38:45,916
[Geng-ming panting] Excuse me.

691
00:38:49,458 --> 00:38:50,874
[keyboard clacking]

692
00:38:50,875 --> 00:38:51,958
LAI WEN-PIN

693
00:38:52,541 --> 00:38:53,832
STATUS: PAID IN FULL

694
00:38:53,833 --> 00:38:55,791
PAID IN FULL

695
00:38:56,750 --> 00:38:57,750
[sighs]

696
00:38:59,125 --> 00:39:00,082
[sighs heavily]

697
00:39:00,083 --> 00:39:03,166
- [Tung-yen] What's up?
- I really gave it to Pi-tan before.

698
00:39:04,583 --> 00:39:06,291
But he actually settled his bills.

699
00:39:07,041 --> 00:39:08,333
I misjudged him.

700
00:39:09,666 --> 00:39:10,875
What should I do?

701
00:39:14,166 --> 00:39:15,375
[Tung-yen breathes deeply]

702
00:39:16,083 --> 00:39:17,833
I lent money to a patient's father.

703
00:39:18,500 --> 00:39:20,290
<i>His daughter got a rare disease,</i>

704
00:39:20,291 --> 00:39:22,582
<i>and he needed to pay out of pocket
for treatment.</i>

705
00:39:22,583 --> 00:39:25,749
<i>Later, when I went to visit the girl,
she wasn't in the children's ward.</i>

706
00:39:25,750 --> 00:39:27,540
<i>In that moment,
I thought I'd been scammed.</i>

707
00:39:27,541 --> 00:39:28,707
[chuckles]

708
00:39:28,708 --> 00:39:32,708
But it turned out the beds were all full
and they'd moved her to a different ward.

709
00:39:33,708 --> 00:39:36,041
Even I make mistakes occasionally.

710
00:39:36,625 --> 00:39:37,457
Yeah?

711
00:39:37,458 --> 00:39:39,415
It's not the mistake that matters.

712
00:39:39,416 --> 00:39:42,250
It's whether you try to find a way
to make up for it or not.

713
00:39:42,875 --> 00:39:44,832
Oh, Tung-yen, you're amazing!

714
00:39:44,833 --> 00:39:47,958
[panting] Thank you! Oh, sign out for me.

715
00:39:48,541 --> 00:39:50,541
- [footsteps departing]
- [exhales sharply]

716
00:39:52,791 --> 00:39:55,999
When you were a little girl
and you had a fever,

717
00:39:56,000 --> 00:39:57,583
this is all you wanted to eat.

718
00:39:58,166 --> 00:40:01,332
And afterwards, you'd perk right back up.

719
00:40:01,333 --> 00:40:03,249
I even bought two boxes.

720
00:40:03,250 --> 00:40:04,583
- Here.
- [chuckles softly]

721
00:40:07,791 --> 00:40:09,791
When you're all better, sweetheart,

722
00:40:11,125 --> 00:40:13,333
don't go back to the ER, okay?

723
00:40:14,333 --> 00:40:15,875
Why are you saying that?

724
00:40:17,291 --> 00:40:19,541
You always wanted to do internal medicine.

725
00:40:21,000 --> 00:40:22,707
You chose the ER

726
00:40:22,708 --> 00:40:25,332
so you'd have more time
to take care of me.

727
00:40:25,333 --> 00:40:26,457
Yeah?

728
00:40:26,458 --> 00:40:28,125
[soft guitar music playing]

729
00:40:28,833 --> 00:40:31,208
But I can't keep dragging you down.

730
00:40:31,791 --> 00:40:32,791
[sniffles]

731
00:40:35,208 --> 00:40:38,625
[shakily] Mom,
you'll never drag me down, okay?

732
00:40:40,166 --> 00:40:41,833
[chuckles softly] Yeah.

733
00:40:43,750 --> 00:40:45,750
[Mrs. Tang crying softly]

734
00:40:46,541 --> 00:40:48,625
[Hsiao-hui]
<i>I wasn't sure what to bring you.</i>

735
00:40:49,666 --> 00:40:51,666
[soft guitar music continues]

736
00:40:53,250 --> 00:40:54,875
I hope you get well soon.

737
00:40:55,875 --> 00:40:58,624
[Hsi]
<i>A patient's daughter visited me today.</i>

738
00:40:58,625 --> 00:41:00,666
<i>She kept thanking me, saying...</i>

739
00:41:01,250 --> 00:41:04,082
her father never would have gotten
the help he needs

740
00:41:04,083 --> 00:41:06,125
if I wasn't working in the ER.

741
00:41:07,500 --> 00:41:09,000
There are some things

742
00:41:09,750 --> 00:41:12,208
that only ER doctors can do.

743
00:41:14,875 --> 00:41:16,875
I've decided to stay there.

744
00:41:17,666 --> 00:41:20,791
If that's... what you really want,

745
00:41:21,500 --> 00:41:23,833
I'll be right here supporting you.

746
00:41:25,416 --> 00:41:26,708
[Hsi exhales sharply]

747
00:41:29,916 --> 00:41:31,249
Here, take this.

748
00:41:31,250 --> 00:41:32,957
Oh, nah.

749
00:41:32,958 --> 00:41:34,207
Hey, come on.

750
00:41:34,208 --> 00:41:36,790
The money would have all flown away
if it wasn't for you.

751
00:41:36,791 --> 00:41:38,999
- Thank you.
- Ah... All right, then.

752
00:41:39,000 --> 00:41:40,333
[laughs] Thank you.

753
00:41:42,250 --> 00:41:44,457
Hi. Hello.

754
00:41:44,458 --> 00:41:45,958
[laughs]

755
00:41:47,625 --> 00:41:50,291
- [dog panting, whines]
- Hey, good boy.

756
00:41:50,833 --> 00:41:51,875
[chuckles]

757
00:41:52,875 --> 00:41:54,040
[Pi-tan groans]

758
00:41:54,041 --> 00:41:55,833
Oh, sorry. Sorry.

759
00:41:56,541 --> 00:41:57,625
Oh! [slurps]

760
00:41:58,208 --> 00:41:59,624
[Pi-tan groans]

761
00:41:59,625 --> 00:42:01,875
[dog barking]

762
00:42:04,125 --> 00:42:06,124
[breathing heavily]

763
00:42:06,125 --> 00:42:07,415
[menacing music playing]

764
00:42:07,416 --> 00:42:10,165
Hey, A-wan.
Where do you think Pi-tan could've gone?

765
00:42:10,166 --> 00:42:12,415
Mingxing Park? Thanks. Bye.

766
00:42:12,416 --> 00:42:14,874
[Pi-tan yelling]
What the hell are you doing? You crazy?

767
00:42:14,875 --> 00:42:16,540
[Pi-tan and Chun-ting groaning]

768
00:42:16,541 --> 00:42:19,290
[Pi-tan]
What is wrong with you? Causing trouble!

769
00:42:19,291 --> 00:42:21,832
- Didn't your parents teach you better?
- Hey!

770
00:42:21,833 --> 00:42:23,999
- [woman crying]
- I'm gonna give you a lesson! You...

771
00:42:24,000 --> 00:42:27,041
- Hey! Pi-tan!
- Fuck you, you little brat!

772
00:42:27,666 --> 00:42:30,083
- [Pi-tan groans]
- Beating up a kid, you crazy?

773
00:42:33,333 --> 00:42:35,790
Is this the kind of thing you do
when you're drinking?

774
00:42:35,791 --> 00:42:37,583
No. No, listen to me.

775
00:42:38,166 --> 00:42:39,499
I saw him with a knife

776
00:42:39,500 --> 00:42:41,790
- trying to rob that girl.
- [screaming]

777
00:42:41,791 --> 00:42:42,874
[Pi-tan] Ah! Watch out!

778
00:42:42,875 --> 00:42:44,166
[knife slashes in flesh]

779
00:42:46,375 --> 00:42:48,375
[ominous music playing]

780
00:42:59,458 --> 00:43:01,458
[closing theme music playing]
